    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f2c61080-0fcd-5088-a538-4903505c8018",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sin\\left(112.5^{\\circ}\\right)+\\cos\\left(112.5^{\\circ}\\right)\\right)^2\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Expand the square and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\nSet $x=112.5^{\\circ}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sin x+\\cos x)^2 &= \\sin^2 x+2\\sin x\\cos x+\\cos^2 x \\\\ &=1+2\\sin x\\cos x \\\\ &=1+\\sin(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sin x\\cos x &=\\sin(2x) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(225^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this exact value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\sin\\left(112.5^{\\circ}\\right)+\\cos\\left(112.5^{\\circ}\\right)\\right)^2&=1+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
